{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/3/context.json","id":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grecolatinovivo-create/emendando-catalogo/manifesti/data/manifesti/romani-pas/440721.json","type":"Manifest","label":{"none":["PAS KENT-1A3D11: Kent-1A3D11. Coin fragment. Siliqua of Arcadius. Obverse view."]},"metadata":[{"label":{"it":["Oggetto"]},"value":{"none":["moneta"]}},{"label":{"it":["Supporto"]},"value":{"none":["metallo (moneta)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Datazione"]},"value":{"none":["383-408 d.C."]}},{"label":{"it":["Provenienza"]},"value":{"none":["contea di ritrovamento: Surrey (Inghilterra e Galles)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Iscrizione o legenda"]},"value":{"none":["[]T[]LT[]"]}},{"label":{"it":["Descrizione"]},"value":{"none":["A fragment of a Roman, struck or hammered, silver, light miliarense or siliqua of Arcadius. Obverse: Draped bust right. Inscription: Illegible. Reverse: VOT? MVLT X? in wreath. Inscription: []T[]LT[]. Die axis: 6 o'clock. Small broken two-thirds of the coin only. Worn with a dark grey patina. This coin dates to 383-408AD. Ref. Coins of England and the UK, Spink 2009, page 65 and Roman Coins and their Values, David R. Sear, 4th Revised Edition, Seaby 1988, page 355-359. The coin fragment is 13.03mm long, 9.51mm wide, 1.3mm thick and weighs 0.6g"]}},{"label":{"it":["Identificativo PAS"]},"value":{"none":["KENT-1A3D11"]}},{"label":{"it":["FindID"]},"value":{"none":["440721"]}}],"requiredStatement":{"label":{"it":["Attribuzione"]},"value":{"it":["Portable Antiquities Scheme / The Trustees of the British Museum (Portable Antiquities Scheme, finds.org.uk). Foto: All rights reserved, Geoff Burr, 2011-05-04 20:12:36, CC BY-SA 4.0 ; All rights reserved, Geoff Burr, 2011-05-04 20:14:18, CC BY-SA 2.0, da Wikimedia Commons. Manifesto scritto da Emendando."]}},"homepage":[{"id":"https://finds.org.uk/database/artefacts/record/id/440721","type":"Text","label":{"none":["PAS KENT-1A3D11: Kent-1A3D11. Coin fragment. Siliqua of Arcadius. Obverse view."]},